# GOLDEN RA RB OVERLAPPING
# GOLDEN-SUBSET RA RB NO
# GROUND-TRUTH: the EPRES fail-closed recogniser, demonstrated rather than
#   asserted. EPRES turns "this element is in the filtered collection" into
#   "this property is PRESENT", which is a fact asserted into UNSAT proofs.
#   It is sound only when a MISSING property makes the filter FALSE.
#
#   Here it does not. `not (dxy > 100)` HOLDS on an electron with no dxy —
#   absence makes the inner comparison a decidable false, so the negation is
#   true — and picky therefore KEEPS dxy-less electrons. If EPRES fired, the
#   frame would carry `size(picky) > 0 => defined(picky[0].dxy)`, EPRED would
#   add `dxy > 2`, and `subset RA within RB` would be PROVEN. It is FALSE:
#   verified with `smash2 run` on an event with one dxy-less electron —
#   RA PASS, RB fail.
#
#   `requires_present` refuses `Not` outright, so no EPRES instance is
#   emitted and no subset is derivable. The companion pin
#   presence_06 is the same file with the `not` removed, where EPRES DOES
#   fire and the subset IS true — so this pair also proves the refusal is
#   the only thing standing between the two.

object picky
  take Ele
  select dxy > 2 or not (dxy > 100)

region RA
  select size(picky) >= 1

region RB
  select dxy(picky[0]) >= -1000
